B = [
('Sony','East Asia','1980s-90s','electronics','In the style of Sony, precise, miniaturised, engineered high-tech design. Compact forms in black or silver with crisp bevelled edges, small softened corners and brushed aluminium faces. Dense, orderly rows of tiny rectangular elements with flat clean sides and deep black bodies. Palette of black, metallic blue and silver with sparing orange accents and small glowing green, amber and blue-green points of light. Lettering is fine, stencil-like capital sans-serif with thin embossed numbers. Later looks drift toward minimal matte black slabs with thin glowing coloured light lines. Mood is technical, exact and aspirational.'),
('Technics','East Asia','1970s-80s','electronics','In the style of Technics, serious, studio-grade, quietly luxurious precision. Wide, flat, low-slung forms in black or silver with thick brushed aluminium faces, heavy knurled-edge round controls and rows of slim evenly spaced rectangular keys. Glossy dark smoked acrylic surfaces, engraved fine scale lines, concentric ring details and illuminated segmented green and amber light bars. Fine, neat white sans-serif lettering and a calm horizontal emphasis. Proportions feel weighty, balanced and professional, with everything squared up and tightly aligned.'),
('Nintendo','East Asia','1980s-present','toys','In the style of Nintendo, playful, approachable, toy-like yet neatly built. Compact rounded rectangles with chunky friendly proportions in glossy and matte plastic. Palette of white, light grey, red and black with bright primary or pastel accents in red, blue, yellow and green, arranged in tidy symmetrical layouts. Vintage looks use cream-grey with dark red trim and gold lettering, later looks use clean white or black slabs with colourful contrasting parts. Cross shapes and small round coloured discs recur as motifs. Rounded sans-serif lettering, often in red. Cheerful and tidy.'),
('Sega','East Asia','1990s','electronics','In the style of Sega, edgy, fast, arcade-bright energy. Glossy black plastic with sharp angular wedge shapes, circular recessed details, moulded ridges and vents, and curved ergonomic forms with oversized round elements. Cobalt blue swirl marks with white and orange accents, loud saturated artwork with bold outlines and hard-edged speed lines, and glowing red or green points of light. A later softer variant is pale off-white and square with a gentle spiral motif. Lettering is slanted bold italic capitals that feel futuristic and quick.'),
('Atari','North America','1970s-80s','electronics','In the style of Atari, warm, retro-futuristic 1970s den character. Heavy wedge-shaped forms clad in simulated dark woodgrain vinyl with black ribbed plastic surfaces, and chunky silver switches lined up along one edge. Thick black rounded controls with a single round red accent on a square base. Palette is warm brown, black and silver, with painted artwork in orange, purple and teal. The mark is a three-bar fan-like symbol in white or red with rounded geometric capitals. Cosy, bulky and optimistic.'),
('Commodore','North America','1980s','electronics','In the style of Commodore, nerdy, hobbyist, cosy 1980s home-tech character. Wide beige or brown-beige plastic with a sloped wedge profile, thick rows of chunky rectangular keys in grey and light brown carrying small coloured graphic symbols, and a rainbow stripe or slim dark band across the surface. Tiny red indicator lights and ribbed vent slots. Cream matching accessories with dark-bezelled boxy forms, blue fields with light-blue borders and blocky pixel text. The mark is a bold angular chevron in stylised capitals.'),
('Olivetti','Europe','1950s-70s','electronics','In the style of Olivetti, playful, elegant, optimistic design treated as sculpture. Soft flowing organic curves in glossy moulded plastic or pressed steel, polished to a gleaming industrial finish. Bright signal red, lemon yellow, teal and orange, with smooth enamelled panels and matching colour throughout. Round-topped white details, recessed rows of tiny coloured elements and small round dials. Lettering is lower-case or rounded sans-serif in white or black, often with a small stripe of colour. Simple shapes, artisanal and joyful.'),
('Bang & Olufsen','Europe','1960s-present','electronics','In the style of Bang & Olufsen, refined, sculptural, serene Scandinavian luxury. Slender, tall, minimalist forms in brushed and polished aluminium, black glass and pale oiled wood, with thin plates that seem to float and tapered cone or pyramid volumes. Fabric surfaces in charcoal or warm grey. Controls are almost invisible, hairline touch strips or a single large circular element, with subtle white or amber light and hidden panels that slide away. Razor-sharp edges with tiny perfectly even gaps. Palette is silver, black, natural oak, dark walnut and occasional soft earthy tones. Lettering is tiny, thin and lowercase.'),
('Leica','Europe','1930s-present','cameras','In the style of Leica, understated, crafted, timeless precision. Compact rectangular forms with a flat top plane, in black enamel or polished silver chrome, wrapped in finely pebbled black leather-like texture. Fine knurled rings, slim barrel-like proportions, engraved white and red numerals and a tiny red dot accent. Brass shows through worn paint on edges, giving honest patina. Minimal, no clutter, with a small white script mark and every control exactly placed.'),
('Hasselblad','Europe','1950s-present','cameras','In the style of Hasselblad, serious, rugged, professional, sculptural. A cubic, square-profiled body in satin black paint with bright chrome trim, or an all-black crinkle texture. Modular blocks clip together with visible seams, large round forms in chrome or black, thin coloured rings and engraved white numerals. Angular crowning shapes and one large simple control. Bold white capital lettering. Special editions use bright colours or exposed carbon weave. Heavy, exact, engineered and block-like.'),
('Polaroid','North America','1970s-80s','cameras','In the style of Polaroid, nostalgic, friendly, snapshot-casual 1970s consumer look. Bulky, sleek, boxy or folding forms in beige, white or black plastic with dark leather-like grip panels, one big circular feature and a bright rectangular accent. Chocolate-brown and tan palette with a rainbow stripe of red, orange, yellow, green and blue, and a big red rectangular control. Square images with a thick white border and a wide bottom margin, glossy, soft warm, slightly faded colour. Bold rounded white sans-serif lettering.'),
('Nikon','East Asia','1960s-80s','cameras','In the style of Nikon, rugged, professional, mechanical. Boxy forms with a raised angular hump on top, in black enamel or silver chrome with finely pebbled leather-like texture. Heavy metal knurled edges, chunky levers and a bold yellow and black stripe accent. Black cylindrical forms with deep rubber-ribbed rings and engraved white, orange and green numerals. Bold white capital lettering on the raised centre. Everything feels tough, dense and made to be used hard.'),
('Canon','East Asia','1970s-80s','cameras','In the style of Canon, dependable, practical, quietly handsome. Compact boxy forms with a black or silver top plane, wood-grain or fine black leather-like covering, and rows of tiny metal dials and small silver buttons. Clean rectangular layout with a large angular crown, round dials and thick levers. Black cylindrical forms with subtle knurling and a thin red ring accent for top-grade pieces. Lettering is a stylised red script mark. Tidy, well-judged and unflashy.'),
('Fujifilm','East Asia','2010s-present','cameras','In the style of Fujifilm, tactile, classic, clean and understated retro-modern design. Compact lean forms with a flat top plane in silver and black, matte black paint over metal and fine textured grips. Many machined aluminium dials with engraved numerals, and chunky rings with engraved scales wrapping round cylinders. A small offset window in one corner, red ruler-like marks and neat black pebbled texture. Lettering is crisp white capitals. Feels hands-on, analogue and calm.'),
('Casio','East Asia','1980s-present','watches','In the style of Casio, cheap, functional, geeky and indestructible. Lightweight resin in black, grey, silver or bright primary colours with squared-off octagonal or rectangular outlines. Grey-green segmented displays with chunky digits, small rubber push controls labelled in tiny white capitals, and tough rubberised protective surrounds. Gold-finished steel variants appear. Grid layouts of controls in grey, orange and blue. Printed text is dense, small and technical with many function labels around the edges. Utilitarian and playful.'),
('Seiko','East Asia','1960s-80s','watches','In the style of Seiko, clean, practical, quietly sophisticated and slightly retro. Stainless steel with sharp faceted edges, mixing polished and brushed surfaces under clear domed glass. Deep blue, black, silver, champagne or sunburst green with fine radial brushing, applied baton markers filled with luminous paint, a small window at three and slim bright hands. Rotating rings with a luminous pip and chunky metal links. Text is small silver capitals and a stylised sans-serif wordmark.'),
('Rolex','Europe','1950s-present','watches','In the style of Rolex, solid, imposing, polished, status-heavy Swiss luxury. Round robust forms in polished and brushed stainless steel or yellow gold with fluted or smooth rims, a protected screw-down feel and a tiny crown motif. A magnifying bubble over a small window. Glossy black, white, blue, green or champagne surfaces with applied polished markers, luminous dots and broad sword-shaped hands. Three-part links with satin centres and polished outer edges. Lettering is crisp small serif capitals in gold or white.'),
('Omega','Europe','1950s-70s','watches','In the style of Omega, purposeful, elegant and exploratory with a vintage space-age touch. Round steel with clean faceted edges, polished or brushed, under domed glass. Black aluminium rings with white scale numerals. Matte black or silver surfaces with contrasting sub-circles, baton hands, applied markers with luminous infill, and a small Greek letter mark at the top. Black leather with white stitching or tapering steel links. Lettering is crisp, slim white sans-serif.'),
('Patek Philippe','Europe','1930s-present','watches','In the style of Patek Philippe, refined, understated, heirloom and timeless haute craft. Slim round or oval forms in polished rose gold, yellow gold or platinum with elegant fine edges, thin rims and hand-stitched alligator leather in brown or black. Cream, silvered or deep blue surfaces with finely guilloched texture, slender leaf-shaped hands, applied gold classical numerals or batons, and discreet small windows. Proportions are clean with every control discreet. Typography is fine serif capitals and delicate cursive.'),
('Nomos Glashutte','Europe','1990s-present','watches','In the style of Nomos Glashutte, spare, precise, calm and modern minimalism. Slim round stainless steel with thin straight edges, a very narrow rim and a flat domed glass over a pure white or silvery-white surface. Slender blued steel hands, thin black numerals in a clean geometric sans-serif, a tiny subsidiary circle and a thin ring track. Plain brown or cordovan leather. Transparent backs reveal a decorated mechanism with stripes and blued screws.'),
('Junghans','Europe','1950s-70s','watches','In the style of Junghans, pared-back, functional and disciplined modernist. Round or rectangular faces with extremely clean layouts, slim baton or simple stick hands, thin black line markers or short numerals in a geometric sans-serif, and gently domed glass. Matte steel or gold with minimal detail. Colours are white, black and grey with occasional warm orange or yellow accents. Small cylinders or squares of off-white enamel or wood with tiny perforation details. Quiet and rational.'),
('Smeg','Europe','1950s-retro','appliances','In the style of Smeg, cheerful, nostalgic, boutique-fashionable retro. Curvaceous rounded rectangles in glossy pastel enamel such as cream, pastel blue, pink, mint green and red, with polished chrome handles, trim and rounded corners. Thick, softly rounded metal edges recall 1950s American automobile styling, with a bold chrome oval mark. Controls are chunky chrome rounds and rounded toggles. Surfaces are shiny and seamless with a soft sheen.'),
('KitchenAid','North America','1930s-present','appliances','In the style of KitchenAid, sturdy, generous, homey with a vintage curve. Heavy cast metal bodies with smooth bulbous curved tops, tilting forms on rear hinges, and tall flat-bottomed steel or glass vessels with curved handles. Glossy enamel in empire red, onyx black, white, pistachio, pastel blue and cream, with polished chrome levers and a round hub at the front. Accessories in brushed silver. Stainless script lettering on the front.'),
('Dyson','Europe','1990s-present','appliances','In the style of Dyson, engineered, futuristic, glossy and rather industrial. Transparent clear plastic reveals inner mechanics against bright coloured plastic parts in purple, fuchsia, yellow, nickel grey and iron. Parts are tubular and ribbed, with exposed engineering, smooth curved moulding, visible fixings and large chunky rounded elements. Thin glossy rings on tall tapering stands replace conventional shapes. Small colour-coded controls and tiny readouts. Lettering is small and bold.'),
('Bosch Professional','Europe','1990s-present','tools','In the style of Bosch Professional, robust, ergonomic, cool and professional. Hard bodies in a distinctive deep blue plastic with black rubberised soft areas and bold red mark accents. Compact shapes with ergonomic curved handles, textured diamond-pattern grips and bright silver metal parts. Labels are crisp white capital sans-serif with small red warning marks. Blue and black pairing repeats everywhere, with tough blue-grey moulded surfaces and silver details.'),
('Makita','East Asia','1990s-present','tools','In the style of Makita, solid, workmanlike and cool teal. Strong teal-blue-green plastic with black rubberised areas, a red stripe accent and tough silver or steel metalwork. Shapes are compact and rounded with chunky proportions, ribbed overmoulded grips and neat rows of small slots. Text is bold white capital lettering with a boxed mark. Bright yellow warning labels as small accents.'),
('DeWalt','North America','1990s-present','tools','In the style of DeWalt, loud, rugged, jobsite-ready and high-visibility. Bright yellow plastic with black rubberised grips and black accent bands, boxy chunky shapes with strong ribbing and protective rubber bumpers. Chunky yellow and black blocks, with small silver steel parts. Text is bold black block capitals on yellow with heavy outlined panels. Yellow and black pairing repeats throughout, rugged and stackable in feel.'),
('Milwaukee Tool','North America','2000s-present','tools','In the style of Milwaukee Tool, aggressive, rugged, masculine and industrial. Signature bright red plastic with black rubberised grips and black blocks, bold stripes of red against black, tough angular shapes with big chunky proportions and reinforced rubber guards. Lettering is large white or black block capitals in a heavy italic sans-serif. Metal parts are raw silver steel. Red and black combine with sturdy, heavy-duty detailing.'),
('Fender','North America','1950s-60s','instruments','In the style of Fender, bright, twangy, sunny California mid-century. Sleek slab forms with offset contours, sunburst finishes fading from yellow through red to black, or solid Surf Green, Daphne Blue, Fiesta Red and cream. White or tortoiseshell panels, chrome hardware, pale maple wood with black dot markers, and a bold curved script mark. Companion surfaces use tweed or black vinyl, silver cloth, chrome corner trim and a row of cream or black round knobs.'),
('Gibson','North America','1950s-60s','instruments','In the style of Gibson, rich, warm, heavy and luxurious. Carved arched forms with a glossy cherry red or golden sunburst finish, cream binding around the edges and a flamed maple figure. Bold mother-of-pearl block or trapezoid inlays on dark rosewood, gold-plated hardware, chrome-covered details, gold barrel shapes and a swept-back crown-like silhouette with a pearl inlay mark. Overall the mood is generous and showy yet refined, with deep saturated colour, warm gloss and a confident sense of heirloom weight.'),
('Marshall Amplification','Europe','1960s-70s','instruments','In the style of Marshall Amplification, loud, stacked, rock and roll and imposing. Large black vinyl-covered volumes with a woven basket-weave cloth front in tan or black, trimmed with gold or silver piping and a bold white script mark on a gold or black panel. A row of chunky black skirted knobs with white numerals, a red jewel lamp and a rocker switch. Tall rectangular blocks stacked like a wall.'),
('Moog Music','North America','1970s','instruments','In the style of Moog Music, warm, vintage, scientific and handcrafted. Solid wood in dark walnut or black with a slanted panel in black or silver, packed with chunky round knobs with white pointers, patch cords and jacks, and small rocker switches. Printed white labels in a clear sans-serif. Long rows of white and black keys. Colour accents are red, orange and white lines grouping sections.'),
('Roland','East Asia','1980s','instruments','In the style of Roland, techy, club-ready and boxy 1980s electronics. Dark grey or black angular metal and plastic with wide control surfaces, rows of tiny coloured plastic buttons in orange, red, blue and cream, slim sliders and small red LED readouts. Rows of small rounded square pads in red, orange, yellow and white. Fine white lettering with grouped panel lines, wedge-like profiles and a bold stripe carrying the name.'),
('Yamaha Synthesizers','East Asia','1980s','instruments','In the style of Yamaha Synthesizers, sleek, digital and early-electronic with soft grey and teal tones. Long slim cream-white or black plastic with flat membrane buttons in grey, a small blue-green backlit display, slim sliders and a full-length keyboard. Silver lettering with a minimal printed grid of function labels, rounded edge corners and a three-pronged fork-like mark. Restrained, tidy and calm.'),
('Teenage Engineering','Europe','2010s-present','instruments','In the style of Teenage Engineering, clean, geeky, graphic and playful. Flat, thin, rectangular aluminium or white plastic slabs with exact grids of small coloured rubber buttons in orange, grey and white, tiny round knobs and bright pixel displays. Orange and neon accents, silkscreened white and black technical lettering in a small monospaced sans-serif, minimal diagrams and fine line graphics. Rounded softness and playful pastel accents.'),
('Nothing','Europe','2020s-present','electronics','In the style of Nothing, stripped-back, nerdy, futuristic and quirky transparent tech. Clear see-through plastic and glass reveal internal components, circuit boards, screws and coils. Palette is white, black and transparent with a signature bright red dot accent. Glowing white light strips arranged in segments around key features. Typography is dot-matrix lettering with round dots forming monochrome numerals, and icons are pixelated. Edges are flat and squared with soft corners.'),
('Samsung','East Asia','2010s-present','electronics','In the style of Samsung, polished, bright, flat-glass and modern. Thin glossy glass slabs with curved edges, metallic frames in black, silver, gold and blue, vivid saturated surfaces and nearly invisible borders. Separate circular details stand out in a tidy vertical or horizontal strip. Thin brushed metal and glossy black or white panels with minimal touch controls. Graphics use rounded square icons, smooth sans-serif type and soft pastel colour gradients.'),
('Xiaomi','East Asia','2010s-present','electronics','In the style of Xiaomi, clean, affordable-minimal and friendly. Simple matte white plastic or glass shapes with softly rounded corners, an orange squared-rounded block mark and small flat circular bumps. Clean minimalist forms in white and light grey with a single glowing coloured ring of light. Graphics use flat colourful icons with soft rounded corners and a friendly sans-serif font. Plain brown cardboard-like neutrals with a single orange square accent.'),
('Bose','North America','1980s-2000s','electronics','In the style of Bose, understated, comfortable and home-friendly. Compact, small rounded boxes and cubes in matte black or white with fabric-covered surfaces, curved or tapering volumes and small clean lettering. Plush rounded soft cushions in black or silver with thin padded bands and subtle buttons. Smooth rounded bodies with a brushed silver face. Surfaces are soft matte and neutral with few visible fixings.'),
('Sonos','North America','2010s-present','electronics','In the style of Sonos, quiet, domestic, matte and minimal. Smooth matte cuboid or cylinder shapes in black or white with perforated metal mesh wrapped around the whole body, and a flat top with a touch-sensitive strip of tiny glowing icons. Soft rounded corners, no visible screws, a small status light and a tiny mark. Long thin horizontal slabs for wide forms.'),
('Zenith Radio','North America','1930s-50s','electronics','In the style of Zenith Radio, polished, elegant and mid-century domestic. Wood with streamlined curved corners and a large round illuminated glass face in cream with black numerals. Bakelite rounds in black or ivory, tall slim fabric panels with gold lines, chrome trim bars and rounded panels. Small curved glass fronts and rounded edges. A lightning bolt Z mark appears at the front.'),
('Philips','Europe','1930s-60s','electronics','In the style of Philips, homely, rounded and optimistic. Wood or bakelite with rounded edges, big round glass faces with illuminated names, and pale ivory or chocolate-brown plastics. Big ribbed round knobs and piano-style keys. Fabric panels with vertical gold slats and a small star and wave mark. Later pieces use bright plastic in cream, mustard and pastel with gently curved forms.'),
('Telefunken','Europe','1950s-60s','electronics','In the style of Telefunken, warm, glowing, heavy and domestic. Polished walnut or beech with rounded fronts, large illuminated glass faces with green and orange glowing accents, and slim ivory keys across the bottom edge. Gold fabric with ornamental slots, chrome-plated trim and big cream knobs. A diamond-shaped mark sits at the front. Rich wood, glowing glass and a heavy, generous presence.'),
('Grundig','Europe','1950s-60s','electronics','In the style of Grundig, solid, warm and middle-class. Wood veneer, brushed gold or chrome keys, large round glass faces with illuminated markers and a glowing green eye, and pale cream or brown plastic knobs. Grey-green hammertone finishes, small meters and neat rows of lettered buttons. A diamond-shaped mark sits on the front. Plain, dependable and built to last, with gentle curves.'),
('Kodak','North America','1900s-80s','cameras','In the style of Kodak, cheerful, familiar and snapshot-friendly. Early forms are leather-covered boxes with a round lens-like feature and a simple window. Mid-century pieces have art deco ribs and chrome stripes, then moulded plastic in the 1970s and 1980s. A bold yellow, red and black colour scheme with big sans-serif lettering and a red stylised K mark. Bright yellow surfaces with red panels.'),
('GoPro','North America','2010s-present','cameras','In the style of GoPro, rugged, active and outdoorsy. Small matte black or dark grey rubberised cubes with a large round glass feature on the front, a tiny screen and a few chunky buttons with white icons. Black plastic frames with chunky tabs, folding prongs, orange-yellow or blue rubber accents and thumb-turned fixings. Transparent protective surfaces. Typography is bold white rounded sans-serif.'),
('Nokia','Europe','1990s-2000s','electronics','In the style of Nokia, tough, friendly and tactile. Chunky forms in blue-grey, black, silver or bright interchangeable coloured plastic, with a small monochrome green-backlit display showing pixel text, a rounded set of soft rubber keys and a prominent curved key in the middle. Short stubby protrusions or smooth rounded cases. Icons are simple pixel images with a friendly rounded font.'),
('Ericsson','Europe','1990s','electronics','In the style of Ericsson, sleek, grey and corporate. Slim grey or black forms with a hinged cover, a small greyish-green display and neat grids of rounded rectangular keys. Cool silver-blue finish, rounded corners and a clean oval mark. Earlier 1950s pieces had a one-piece curved bakelite body in ivory, black or red. Cool, tidy and businesslike. Surfaces stay smooth and uncluttered, with restrained colour, even spacing and a calm, professional mood.'),
('Motorola','North America','1980s-2000s','electronics','In the style of Motorola, bold, tech-era and metallic. The 1980s look is huge and cream-grey with a chunky rectangular grid of large grey keys, a bright red-orange LED display and heavy black elements. The 2000s look is razor-thin with a brushed aluminium finish, a flat grid etched from a single metal sheet and a blue backlight glow. A stylised M bat-wing mark.'),
('Lenovo ThinkPad','East Asia','1990s-present','computers','In the style of Lenovo ThinkPad, serious, utilitarian and corporate. Matte black soft-touch surfaces with square corners and a flat slab shape, a red rubber nub accent, scooped matte black keys with white letters and a red-dot accent. Red-trimmed details, minimal silver trim, flat joints and small status lights. Italic white text spells the name. Mood is sober and dependable, with black dominating, red used as one tiny deliberate accent, no ornament and everything built for work.'),
('Vitsoe','Europe','1960s-present','furniture','In the style of Vitsoe, calm, minimalist and timeless. Thin vertical aluminium lines with slim aluminium planes hung from them on small pegs. Surfaces are powder-coated in white, black or light grey, or smooth plywood in pale birch, with sleek clean edges. Crisp panels in matte pale colours with narrow slots and small detailing. Everything is clean, orderly and rectilinear with thin lines and no decoration.'),
('Harley-Davidson','North America','1940s-present','motorcycles','In the style of Harley-Davidson, rumbling, rebellious open-road Americana. Heavy forms with a low long silhouette, deep chrome plating, fat teardrop volumes in gloss black, orange or deep red with a small bar-and-shield emblem and pinstripe scrolls, wide valanced curves and big round forms. Fringed black leather, tall flared lines, polished fins and chunky riveted details. Mood is heavy, loud and swaggering, with black and chrome dominating and ornament worn proudly.'),
('Indian Motorcycle','North America','1930s-40s','motorcycles','In the style of Indian Motorcycle, rich, gleaming art deco Americana. Enormous deep valanced skirted curves, flowing teardrop volumes, glossy deep red paint with cream or gold pinstripes and hand-lettered script, bright chrome, a small lit ornament, tan leather with springs, long sweeping curves and polished fins. Lacquer colours such as Indian red, ivory and dark blue. Mood is lavish, streamlined and proud, with ornament and sweeping curves used generously.'),
('Triumph Motorcycles','Europe','1960s','motorcycles','In the style of Triumph Motorcycles, nostalgic British cafe-racer attitude. Compact, lean, forward-leaning proportions with small tapered volumes and a short, tight stance. Polished metal and chrome set against bright enamel colour such as silver, blaze yellow, red and pastel blue, with thin white pinstripes and a small neat enamel badge. Round, simple forms, ribbed black upholstery, fine spoked circles and mechanical detail left visible. Honest, hand-built, a little rebellious.'),
('Ducati','Europe','1990s-present','motorcycles','In the style of Ducati, fast, sculpted, muscular racing-bred Bologna look. Glossy Italian red with white or black accents, exposed tubular structure in red, visible cooling fins, sharply tapered forms with aggressive paired lights, a short tail with a bold racing stripe, gold or black multi-spoke circles and drilled details. Muscular, stacked and mechanical. Mood is intense, athletic and passionate, with red dominating and every shape pulled tight over the structure.'),
('Vespa','Europe','1950s-60s','scooters','In the style of Vespa, soft rounded one-piece shell forms in smooth pressed steel, wasp-waisted curves, enclosed side panels and bulbous shielding shapes, small wheels, chrome trim strips, pastel enamel paint in mint green, cream, sky blue, coral and ivory, and a single curved bench in two-tone vinyl. Playful 1950s-60s Italian holiday charm. Surfaces are smooth and seamless, with a cheerful, lightweight, sunny mood.'),
('Lambretta','Europe','1950s-60s','scooters','In the style of Lambretta, mod-era 1960s chic with minimal curves and clean engineering. Slim angular silhouette with tubular structure, flat-sided panels and straight horizontal lines, an exposed rounded cover, tall narrow forms with integrated lamps, two-tone paint in grey, blue, cream and red, polished alloy and chrome details, thin lines and racing stripes. Mood is sharp, youthful and stylish, with a lean, tidy, engineered look and restrained ornament.'),
('Honda Super Cub','East Asia','1960s-present','motorcycles','In the style of Honda Super Cub, friendly, cheerful and utilitarian. Small step-through form with a pressed-steel spine, large clear plastic surfaces, rounded lamps, deep scalloped curves, a flat bench in black vinyl, small horizontal engine forms with silver cases, and small white or red hubs. Solid cheerful colours such as red, white, pale blue and bright yellow with simple minimal graphics.'),
('Kawasaki','East Asia','1970s-80s','motorcycles','In the style of Kawasaki, aggressive muscle stance with racing-flag styling. Bold lime green paint as the signature colour, angular volumes with white and black stripes, square-edged covers, large air-cooled black finned forms, four-into-four chrome pipes, half fairings, bold sporty decals, stout rubber-gaitered parts and cast or spoke wheels. Loud, fast and show-off, bold and brash. Colour is saturated and unapologetic, with high-contrast graphics and an angular, aggressive attitude.'),
('Royal Enfield','South Asia','1950s-present','motorcycles','In the style of Royal Enfield, honest, rugged vintage British-Indian character. Rounded heavy build, deep teardrop volumes in gloss black, deep green, maroon or cream with pinstripes and a circular badge with a cannon emblem, upright round chrome forms, a single long chrome tube, polished alloy covers, upright lines, a sprung single tan or black saddle, big mudguards and wire spoke wheels.'),
('Brough Superior','Europe','1920s-30s','motorcycles','In the style of Brough Superior, understated aristocratic racing elegance and fine craftsmanship. Hand-built, long, low, sleek silhouette, nickel-plated surfaces with black lining, polished nickel and black enamel finish, gleaming exposed mechanical forms, slim curves, copper details, leather on springs and brass accents. Everything is slender, exacting and hand-finished and quietly rare. Mood is quiet, aristocratic and precise, with gleaming metal, black contrast and rare, bespoke refinement.'),
('Moto Guzzi','Europe','1970s','motorcycles','In the style of Moto Guzzi, smooth, solid, clean lines with a long low stance. Big transverse 90 degree V-twin forms whose two heads stick out sideways, polished shaft drive, red frame or dark bodywork, teardrop volumes in Italian red, silver, black or green with a small eagle emblem, chrome pipes, cast wheels and a touring seat. Mood is calm, stout and confident, with generous proportions, honest mechanical forms left visible and polished metal against saturated colour.'),
('BSA','Europe','1950s-60s','motorcycles','In the style of BSA, solid, utilitarian British classic. Sturdy profile, bright finishes in polished chrome and cherry red, black or sunshine yellow, badges of three rifles in a circle, rounded volumes with chrome side panels, a big lamp housing, valanced curves, bulky air-cooled forms in silver, wire wheels, upright lines and a ribbed dual seat. Honest, hardy and plain-spoken.'),
]
